course: dictionary
lesson: 15929
title: Unreadable: writing, books, faces and files
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unreadable means you cannot read it, or it is very hard to read. Something can be unreadable in four ways: the writing is too messy, faded or tiny to read; a book is so badly written that you cannot keep going; a face shows no feelings, so you cannot tell what someone thinks; or a computer cannot open a file.
explain: «The old letter was faded, and the ink was almost unreadable.» The clue is faded: the ink has gone so pale that the words cannot be seen. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "too pale to read" still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: «His face gave nothing away. It was an unreadable expression.» Here you cannot read words at all, you read a face. Unreadable means you cannot tell what the person is feeling or thinking. Look at the clues around the word: gave nothing away tells you the face was blank.
fact: Unreadable is an adjective. It is made from un- (not), read, and -able (able to be).
fact: «Unreadable» means so messy, faded or small that you cannot read it.
fact: «Unreadable» can also mean so boring or badly written that it is hard to keep reading.
fact: «An unreadable expression» means a face that shows no feeling, so you cannot tell what the person thinks.
fact: On a computer, an unreadable file is one that cannot be opened.
exercise: «The notes from the teacher were so smudged that Mia could not read a single word.» What does unreadable mean here? | Very loud | Very funny | Brand new and shiny | *Too messy to read
exercise: «Ben said the book was unreadable, so he put it back on the shelf.» What does unreadable suggest about the book? | Written in gold ink | Too heavy to lift | *So badly written that it was hard to keep reading | Full of coloured pictures
exercise: Which example uses unreadable to describe a face? | The letter was unreadable and faded | *His face was an unreadable expression | The file was unreadable | The ink was unreadable
test: «The screen said the memory stick held an unreadable file.» What does an unreadable file mean on a computer? | A file that is written in another language | A file that has been printed twice | *A file the computer cannot open | A file with lots of pictures
test: Which word means the opposite of unreadable? | Unhappy | *Readable | Unfriendly | Invisible
exam: «The old map was so faded that its words were ___.» Choose the best word to fill the gap. | ancient | loud | empty | *unreadable
